# ==============================================================================
# Example 55: Xenobacter alienus — Complex Synthetic Organism Ecosystem
# ==============================================================================
#
# Organism: Xenobacter alienus (synthetic)
# Design:   A hypothetical heterotroph with glycolysis, TCA, PPP,
#           fermentation (lactate overflow), and anaplerosis.
#           24 genes across 5 metabolic pathways.
#
# Genome:
#   Glycolysis:       glk, pfkA, pgi, tpiA, gapA, pgk, gpmA, eno, pykF
#   TCA cycle:        gltA, acnB, icd, sucAB, sucCD, sdhCDAB, fumB, mdh
#   Pentose phosphate: zwf, gnd, rpiA
#   Fermentation:     ldhA
#   Anaplerosis:      ppc
#
# Kinetic parameters: BRENDA EC-class medians for each enzyme.
# EcGEM: 42-reaction E. coli core model with 24 enzyme constraints.
#
# Environment: Glucose minimal medium, 37C, pH 7.0, aerobic.
#
# Expected results:
#   Growth rate:  ~4.2 h^-1 (enzyme unconstrained)
#   Batch yield:  ~0.23 gDW/mmol glucose
#   Essential:    pfkA, gltA, icd, sucAB, gapA, eno, zwf, ppc, NADH_OX
#   Dispensable:  pykF (100%), ldhA (50%), glk (33%)
#
# Run: helixlang examples/55_custom_organism_ecosystem.helix
# ==============================================================================

